            "text": "{\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"If an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee, including employees exempt from the FLSA recordkeeping requirements (such as bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees defined in 29 CFR part 541), the employer bears the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Regardless of whether an employer maintains accurate records of hours worked, an employer must be able to clearly demonstrate that full-time teachers (as defined in § 825.102) of an elementary or secondary school system, institution of higher education, or other educational establishment or institution (who often work outside the classroom or at home) did not work 1,250 hours during the previous 12 months in order to claim that they are not eligible for FMLA leave.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"background\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Provides a cross-reference directing readers to § 825.801(d) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees, conveying no independent substantive duty in this passage.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
